scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: house-md
run_id: 1
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 13
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 35.1
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. Reviewer
    flagged F5 (env override swallowing) but not the file-loading equivalent. TEA
    config tests exist but don't assert that parse/permission errors propagate distinctly
    from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer verified CWE-209 for ServerError and Unauthorized Display impls,
    but did not flag Io(#[error(transparent)]) forwarding full OS error details. No
    main.rs exists (F2) so the eprintln pattern isn't present yet, but the transparent
    Io variant in the error type was not flagged.
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote header injection tests for newlines in tenant/token. Dev implemented
    sanitize_header_value stripping CR/LF. Reviewer verified CWE-113 prevention. However,
    the deeper type-safety issue (raw String vs TenantId from axiathon-core) was not
    flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding F7: ''clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs, reqwest,
    and toml are specified inline with version numbers rather than as workspace dependencies...
    risking version fragmentation across the workspace.'''
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding F4: ''RawConfig uses default serde deserialization,
    which silently ignores unknown fields... If someone puts token = "secret" in the
    TOML, serde silently drops it... #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] should be used.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the vacuously true assertion pattern. Reviewer's F4 mentions
    the token test is vacuous due to hardcoded has_token_from_file(), but does not
    identify the specific is_none() || true pattern that makes the assertion always
    pass.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test. TEA wrote config tests but the
    specific test with 'let _ = config;' and no assert_eq! checks on server()/token()
    was not identified as vacuous by any phase.
